  "notes": "{氾濫|はんらん} is used both literally for floods and figuratively for excessive spread.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n- {氾|はん} (overflow) + {濫|らん} (excessive, rampant)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {洪水|こうずい}: flood (general term)\n- {決壊|けっかい}: dam/levee breach\n- {浸水|しんすい}: flooding, submersion\n- {冠水|かんすい}: submersion (roads, fields)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {氾濫|はんらん}{危険|きけん}{水位|すいい}: flood danger water level\n- {氾濫|はんらん}{警戒|けいかい}: flood warning\n- {情報|じょうほう}の{氾濫|はんらん}: information overload",
